The program is an implementation of a weak head normal form parser  using a call by name path which tries to evaluate an expression  tree representing a lambda calculus term.

The grammer we use to express our lambda term is:
term := LAMBDA LCID DOT  term | application
application := application atom | atom
atom := LPAREN term RPAREN | LCID
The program will parse a lambda expression according to the grammer above.Because the grammer is recursively defined , the functions parsing the expressions will call each other 
recursively as they recognize parts of the lambda expression.This makes a recursive-descent parser which cannot handle left recursion but the left recursion can has been removed
 (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Left_recursion)
During parsing the nodes are assigned de brujin indices to avoid variable capture during the substitution process.When the lambda expression tree is created it is then evaluated.The 
approach implemented is to reduce the leftmost redex first where a redex is just an abstraction.When variables are captured we use S to signify a substitution  should be done.


